<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24510" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">interventor</span></b> , ōris, m.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>One who comes in</i>, <i>a
			visitor</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vacuus ab interventoribus dies,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fat. 1, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A surety</i>, <i>bondsman</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si filius fidejussor, vel quasi interventor
					acceptus sit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					15, 1, 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>An intercessor</i>, <i>mediator</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Lampr. Comm. 4</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
